# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A definition body carries the kind of definition holding it"

# TiddlyWiki keeps four definition pragmas and stores each body verbatim, stamping which kind it
# holds — fnprocdef.js sets isFunctionDefinition, isProcedureDefinition or isWidgetDefinition, and
# macrodef.js sets none of them. The kind decides what LANGUAGE the body carries, and the four
# differ:
#
#   function   the body reaches the FILTER engine — widget.js calls filterTiddlers on it
#   procedure  the body reads as wikitext, its parameters arriving as variables
#   widget     the body reads as wikitext, its parameters arriving as variables
#   define     the body reads as wikitext after textual parameter substitution
#
# A body scope naming the wrong kind names the wrong language. It also reaches an author directly:
# writing tiddlers on disk and troubleshooting the wiki built from them means reading the same
# definition in two places, and a one-line function that colours as a macro body on disk reads as
# a different construct from the one the wiki runs.
#
# The block forms carry the kind already. These pin the one-line forms beside them.

! A one-line function body reads as a function body

\function f.one(a) [tag[Task]]
#                  ^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.variable.function.body.tiddlywiki5

! A one-line procedure body reads as a procedure body

\procedure p.one(a) go
#                   ^^ meta.variable.procedure.body.tiddlywiki5

! A one-line widget body reads as a widget body

\widget $my.one(a) go
#                  ^^ meta.variable.widget.body.tiddlywiki5

! A one-line define body reads as a macro body, because a define defines a macro

\define d.one(a) go
#                ^^ meta.variable.macro.body.tiddlywiki5

! A multiline body of each kind keeps the name it already carried

\function f.many(a)
[tag[Task]]
#^^^^^^^^^^ meta.variable.function.body.tiddlywiki5
\end

\procedure p.many(a)
go
#^ meta.variable.procedure.body.tiddlywiki5
\end

\widget $my.many(a)
go
#^ meta.variable.widget.body.tiddlywiki5
\end
